The emulator tier (emu/) is implemented clean from primary specifications
only — the ARM Architecture Reference Manual, Acorn MEMC/VIDC/IOC
documentation, and RISC OS behaviour from the Apache-2.0-licensed ROOL
sources and the RISC OS 5 PRMs. The following works were studied as
behaviour reference and are credited here; no code or pseudocode-level
material is derived from them (spec section 5 derivation boundary):

  * RPCEmu (GPL v2) by Sarah Walker and Peter Howkins
    https://www.marutan.net/rpcemu/index.php — reference and credit only.
  * RPCEmu Extended (GPL v2 fork) by Andrew Timmins
    https://github.com/andrewtimmins/rpcemu-extended — reference and credit
    only; its licence-boundary precedent (ROOL's Apache-2.0/BSD USB modules
    carried as guest-ROM data, never linked) is followed for ROM images and
    Wi-Fi firmware blobs.
  * Arculator (freeware, closed source) — Archimedes-era behaviour
    reference only; its code is never read or copied.
  * ROOL RISC OS 5 sources (Apache-2.0) and RISC OS 5 PRMs — behavioural
    reference for RISC OS semantics.
  * MAME (mamedev) Acorn device drivers (acorn_memc/acorn_vidc/acorn_ioc)
    — used only for hardware register-layout facts (addresses, bit
    fields), which are not copyrightable expression.

RISC OS ROM images and Broadcom/Cypress Wi-Fi firmware blobs are runtime
loaded data acquired separately under their own terms; they are not part
of this distribution and are not licensed under the Apache License.
